<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scupi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Scupi was an ancient city on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar">Vardar</a>, just north-west of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skopje">Skopje</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>. Originally a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dardanians">Dardani</a>, it became a Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> base and then, under the Flavian emperors, a colony of veterans, later serving as capital of the province of Dardania. An earthquake destroyed it in 518, and its ruins have been excavated since the 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scupi.jpg" alt="Scupi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dimitar Georgievski · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skopje_and_Skupi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
